WEBVTT

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.360
<i>Hanamaru Kindergarten</i>

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.250
Isn't it interesting?

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.260
You think so?

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.060
The heroines overcome various obstacles of love to be united with their lovers!

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.630
Isn't love wonderful?

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:53.230
The settings and stories aren't realistic at all.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.170
There's nothing special about these comic books.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.130
What does Tsuchi think he's saying?

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:04.760
Even I know the difference between reality and fiction!

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:07.130
I'm not an idiot!

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.190
I just wanted to tell him indirectly...

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.110
...that's the kind of romance I want to have with him!

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.040
That may have been too indirect for him to notice.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.920
Poor Anzu-chan.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:19.820
You're being naive!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.500
Don't do that!

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.130
Naive, Anzu!

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:27.680
Those fantastic romantic developments will never actually happen...

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.370
...but people can't help but hope for them anyway.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.440
Someday a girl will fall out of the sky for a lame guy like me.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:50.370
A handsome man will pick up my book of poems, and he'll date a plain girl like me.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.620
I'm not plain.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:56.780
Tsuchida-sensei must also have a dream like this.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:03.900
Therefore, you must fulfill his hopes...

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.260
...by producing the romance of his dreams!

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.930
The romance of his dreams!

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:15.680
I should take him out on a fantastic date.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:18.910
For example, you could meet him like this.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.670
Sounds like fun.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.230
"A Hanamaru Date"

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:27.580
Today I'd like to ask you out on a wonderful date!

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.020
A date?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.080
I'll meet you at the bench in the yard at one o'clock.

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:43.210
She should be showing up soon.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.690
Sorry.

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:47.820
There was a bit of traffic.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.640
I hope you didn't wait long, Tsuchida-san.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:54.820
So that's what you're up to.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.710
No, I just got here too.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.690
Oh, good.

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:01.740
The weather's nice today, isn't it?

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:03.510
It certainly is.

00:04:04.290 --> 00:04:06.050
By the way, whose clothes are those?

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.510
I borrowed this from Chichan-sensei.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.340
When I told her I was going on a date, she lent it to me.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.620
Here you go!

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.380
So it was Kawashiro-sensei...

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.760
Why is she always playing games with me?

00:04:17.950 --> 00:04:21.540
Tsuchida-san, I know of a wonderful café.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.180
Would you like to check it out?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.050
Sure.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:30.380
Tsuchida-san, how many sugars do you take in your coffee?

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.890
You don't need to go out of your way to sound like an adult just because we're on a date.

00:04:35.260 --> 00:04:39.650
Really? I thought that was taking it too far, too.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.230
This bakery's tiramisu is delicious.

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:47.190
Really?

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.940
And don't you think this place has a great atmosphere?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.750
It's an open-air café.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:53.540
You're right.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.290
Tsuchida, are you on a date?

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:56.480
Way to go!

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.530
You'd better be treating her!

00:04:59.690 --> 00:05:01.360
Get out of here.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.750
What a cute girlfriend you have.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.840
We'd like to offer the lovely couple something on the house.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.340
On the house?

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:13.060
I wonder what it is, Tsuchi.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:16.260
It's our tropical drink.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.100
Is this the milk left over from lunch?

00:05:21.260 --> 00:05:25.370
Oh, no! There's two straws. What are we going to do?

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.960
Well, there's no point in letting it go to waste.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:55.860
Okay, let's drink it.

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.460
Tsuchi!

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.980
Oh, sorry! I was thirsty.

00:06:04.010 --> 00:06:05.780
Are you okay, Anzu-chan?

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.060
It's all Tsuchi's fault.

00:06:08.060 --> 00:06:08.560
Anzu-chan...

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:13.450
We were on a date. We were supposed to have it together.

00:06:08.890 --> 00:06:09.600
I'm sorry.

00:06:14.390 --> 00:06:16.800
Tsuchida-sensei's just embarrassed.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:18.530
Is that true?

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.520
Tsuchida-sensei's not used to going on dates.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.920
Not used to dating...

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:26.280
But, but...

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:28.720
S-sorry. It's my fault.

00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:30.830
Really?

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.590
Really. It's my fault.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:35.030
I'm sorry.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:36.540
Tsuchi...

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.510
...do you like me?

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:43.490
Do you?

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.850
I've got to watch what I say, or she'll start crying again.

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:50.500
Of course I like you.

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:53.760
The way a teacher likes a student.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:07:00.570
Hooray!

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.120
Good for you, Anzu-chan.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.570
Good for you.

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:03.790
Let's go on a drive next!

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:05.410
A drive?

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:10.650
Did I say something I shouldn't have?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.700
Having fun, Anzu?

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:22.100
Yes!

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.600
Really? Great.

00:07:31.150 --> 00:07:34.680
Looks like you're having fun, Anzu-chan.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.100
Are you going somewhere with Tsuchida-sensei?

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.080
I'm on a date with Tsuchi.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:41.420
Is that so? How wonderful.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.200
"A little disappointed"

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:48.200
Looking good, Anzu-chan.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.110
That sweater looks great on you.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.210
Thank you.

00:07:54.500 --> 00:07:57.820
Tsuchi, it's starting to get dark.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.330
Come sit with me.

00:08:05.570 --> 00:08:06.870
How long will this keep going?

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:12.720
This park has a great atmosphere at night.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.840
Look at all the stars.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:20.760
See?

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.630
What a great mood.

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:26.250
Almost there...

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.010
Afternoon playtime's over in five minutes.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.100
Hey, look!

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:32.640
Look at that!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:33.910
What is it now?

00:08:34.460 --> 00:08:35.830
It's a shooting star.

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:38.000
Twinkle, twinkle.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.120
Twinkle, twinkle.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:43.380
Twinkle, twinkle.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.290
Pretty clever.

00:08:46.030 --> 00:08:47.640
I bet I could turn this into something fun for the kids.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.640
They say if you wish upon a shooting star, your wish will come true.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:56.410
I wish for Tsuchi and I to be together forever.

00:08:56.780 --> 00:08:59.730
May your dreams come true.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.890
Twinkle, twinkle.

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:05.140
Make a wish too, Tsuchi.

00:09:07.130 --> 00:09:09.040
"What is the teacher's wish?"

00:09:09.850 --> 00:09:10.890
Oh, right.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.180
Let's see...

00:09:15.560 --> 00:09:18.580
I wish for everyone in the world to be happy.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.910
That's not what I meant!

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.280
In that case...

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:28.340
I wish to play Dragon Quest VII on my DS.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.490
Way to ruin the mood.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.020
Did you know, young man?

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:37.520
This park has a bit of a legend.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:40.900
That bench you're sitting on.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:45.780
Couples that kiss there stay together forever.

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:48.290
Go for it!

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:50.320
Listen...

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:57.460
It's easy to refuse this one, but I'm sure she'd cry again.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.180
Playtime is over.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.560
Please return to your classrooms.

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.460
Playtime is over, everyone!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:11.510
Okay!

00:10:15.420 --> 00:10:17.730
Time for our end of the day meeting.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.010
After that, I've got to prepare for tomorrow.

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:25.890
I don't want to go home tonight.

00:10:25.990 --> 00:10:29.080
You've got to pack up your things for when your mother gets here.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:34.450
You're doing it wrong! You should be getting a hotel room or taking me to a bar!

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.960
Sounds like you've got it all planned out.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:41.340
Because... because...

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:42.460
Today...

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:44.730
Today...

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.670
...I had a lot of fun thanks to you, Anzu.

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:53.260
We can continue this later.

00:10:56.250 --> 00:10:56.870
Okay.

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:16.200
Hiiragi is a chicken, and Koume is a rabbit.

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:23.090
"Zoo"

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.550
Aren't you going to be an animal, too?

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:22.630
Let's pick up where we left off!

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.760
Let's keep going.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.010
We're not done with our date.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:29.500
Oh, Anzu-chan.

00:11:30.760 --> 00:11:32.910
Are you on a date with Tsuchida-sensei today, too?

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.480
Yes. We're going to the zoo.

00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:40.170
No, no. That's not it at all.

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:41.640
That's exactly what we're doing.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:54.060
I will be attending a relative's wedding, so I won't be here tomorrow.

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:59.130
Tsuchida-sensei won't be here tomorrow.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:03.040
I want to have a wedding with Tsuchi!

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:05.670
Now, now...

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:11.110
Anzu, don't cause any trouble for Yamamoto-sensei tomorrow.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.610
Yamamoto-sensei?

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:17.300
Yamamoto-sensei is going to be looking after the Sakura Class just for tomorrow.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:21.650
Make sure you help her out in any way you can, class.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.610
Okay.

00:12:24.030 --> 00:12:24.770
Okay.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:29.080
A whole day with Yamamoto-sensei...

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:33.850
A battle for love between Anzu and Yamamoto-sensei.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.040
"A Hanamaru Helper"

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:42.660
I'd recommend this picture book.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.210
Nana-chan, I heard you're looking after the Sakura Class today.

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:48.260
Will you be okay? Do you need any help?

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:50.970
Thank you.

00:12:51.520 --> 00:12:53.730
I'll let you know if I do.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:55.220
Yamamoto-sensei.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.450
Will you be running back and forth between two classes?

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:03.730
Since the weather's so nice, I was hoping to use the wooden deck.

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:07.300
The wooden deck? What a great idea.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.970
I'm sure the Sakura Class already heard about it yesterday...

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:16.120
...but Tsuchida-sensei isn't here today.

00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:20.370
Today, we'll be combining the Sakura and Peach Classes.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:24.410
Let's have fun together in this special classroom.

00:13:24.470 --> 00:13:25.580
Okay.

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:27.980
It feels great out here.

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:28.650
Yeah.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:31.220
Our classroom has a sky.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.510
You're right.

00:13:40.220 --> 00:13:42.250
We'll be having class with the sun today.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:43.190
Okay.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.430
Since Tsuchi isn't here, I'll help you.

00:13:48.820 --> 00:13:49.830
You will, Anzu-chan?

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:52.390
Are you sure, Anzu-chan?

00:13:53.210 --> 00:13:54.050
What do you mean?

00:13:54.280 --> 00:13:58.010
You know how Tsuchida-sensei feels about Yamamoto-sensei...

00:13:58.270 --> 00:14:01.800
But Tsuchi told us to help her.

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.870
We've got to give her a hand.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:06.230
Anzu-san certainly is positive.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.080
What an unexpected development.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:11.500
So give me lots of work to do.

00:14:12.010 --> 00:14:17.310
I guess I'll accept your offer and have you help me.

00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:18.910
Leave it to me.

00:14:18.910 --> 00:14:20.790
Wow, Anzu-chan.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:21.900
You can do it!

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:25.190
Yamamoto-sensei, what should I do?

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:26.810
Let's see...

00:14:27.590 --> 00:14:29.940
Why don't we fold some origami together?

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:33.820
Anzu-chan, let's get some colored paper from the Peach Classroom.

00:14:34.530 --> 00:14:36.410
I can get it all by myself.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:37.450
Are you sure?

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.170
It's no problem at all.

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:47.960
Let's see... colored paper.

00:14:48.510 --> 00:14:49.470
Is it in here?

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.130
Is it in here?

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.270
It's not here either.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:07.900
What's taking Anzu-chan so long?

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:11.350
I wonder what she's up to.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:14.250
You're right. I'll go check on her.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.600
What's wrong?

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:25.710
I thought you might not know where we keep the colored paper.

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:28.230
It was no problem. I found it.

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:31.590
Why don't you hand some out to everyone?

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:32.500
Okay.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:34.740
Give three sheets to each person, okay?

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:35.920
Got it.

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:45.460
Hey, how are you supposed to fold this?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:46.790
I don't get it at all.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.010
How are everyone's tulips coming along?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:50.850
I did it!

00:15:51.640 --> 00:15:53.490
Me too!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.900
Good work.

00:16:03.140 --> 00:16:05.060
Thank you for the tea.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.310
You're welcome.

00:16:07.700 --> 00:16:09.080
Let me pour the tea!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:17.990
Having lunch outdoors make me feel like we're on a hiking trip.

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:19.150
Doesn't it?

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:22.890
Let me help you more.

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.810
Give me more jobs to do.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.890
Why don't we play dodge ball in the yard next?

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.270
Dodge ball? Sounds great.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:35.200
Why don't you get some balls from the storage room?

00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:35.980
Roger that!

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:42.220
Let's see... dodge ball.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:43.790
There it is.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:46.640
Hurry, hurry...

00:16:50.220 --> 00:16:52.210
I got the dodge balls!

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.490
Well done.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:56.890
We've got this!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:16:58.030
Let's go!

00:17:00.970 --> 00:17:03.140
Anzu-chan, sorry to ask you for a favor in the middle of the match...

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:07.440
...but do you think you could watch everyone while I'm gone? I'll be back soon.

00:17:07.570 --> 00:17:09.430
You need to use the bathroom?

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:11.810
I can take care of things here.

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:24.060
Good bye, sensei.

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:26.790
Good bye, everyone.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.430
See you tomorrow, class.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:35.540
What an exhausting day of work.

00:17:36.100 --> 00:17:38.090
I worked really hard today.

00:17:38.710 --> 00:17:40.240
Wow, Anzu-chan.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.050
Hey, working woman.

00:17:42.570 --> 00:17:45.400
Your mothers are waiting, class.

00:17:45.400 --> 00:17:46.550
Okay.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.200
Yamamoto-sensei, do you still have work to do?

00:17:58.710 --> 00:18:01.130
I have to clean up and prepare for tomorrow.

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:02.420
It's not too much.

00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:06.580
Wait one minute.

00:18:11.610 --> 00:18:13.030
Yamamoto-sensei.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.620
I'm going to keep helping you.

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:19.300
You've already helped me plenty today.

00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:21.010
You don't need to do any more.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:25.040
I promised I would help you, so I'm not leaving until you're finished.

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:30.560
I talked to my mommy, and she said she would come by later to pick me up.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:34.190
In that case, I accept your offer.

00:19:11.110 --> 00:19:12.480
What is it, Anzu-chan?

00:19:12.670 --> 00:19:14.240
N-nothing.

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:23.310
Yamamoto-sensei is beautiful.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.050
Are you feeling tired, Anzu-chan?

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.680
You did a lot of work today.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:42.340
Yamamoto-sensei, you're beautiful and kind.

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.310
You'll take Tsuchi from me.

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:50.700
Thank you...

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.780
...but you're cuter than me.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:58.350
I'm sure Tsuchida-sensei loves you too.

00:19:58.800 --> 00:19:59.850
Really?

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:05.080
But I'm still young...

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:11.030
I might be an adult, but I still cause a lot of trouble for Tsuchida-sensei and Kusano-sensei...

00:20:11.260 --> 00:20:15.040
...making mistakes and losing things.

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:16.330
Really?

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:17.130
Yes.

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:23.370
I'm so grateful you helped me today, Anzu-chan.

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:25.550
Thank you.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:32.310
I'll help you again sometime.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:35.050
Don't hesitate to ask for anything, okay?

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:38.530
Promise.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:44.100
...and Tsuchi is always playing games.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:45.500
Is that so?

00:20:45.690 --> 00:20:49.320
And he doesn't like onions, so he never eats them.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.190
That's no good.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:54.770
Yamamoto-sensei, do you like anyone?

00:20:54.890 --> 00:20:57.820
I love everyone at the kindergarten.

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.840
That's not what I meant.

00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:07.200
I hope they didn't get in too much trouble yesterday.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:13.820
The bride sure was beautiful.

00:21:15.450 --> 00:21:17.810
Someday, that'll be me and Yamamoto-sensei...

00:21:24.180 --> 00:21:27.170
I like mille feuille.

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:29.080
Mille feuille is good, too.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.100
I like mont blanc.

00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:36.110
The other day, I went to that new store with my brother.

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:38.910
The cake buffet?

00:21:39.200 --> 00:21:40.240
Yes.

00:21:39.530 --> 00:21:42.390
Sounds like they're excited about something.

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:45.460
Cake buffet? Is that a place where you can eat...

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.120
Good morning.

00:21:46.040 --> 00:21:47.430
What are you talking about?

00:21:47.840 --> 00:21:52.120
We're having girl talk! It's not for boys!

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:53.590
No boys allowed.

00:21:54.400 --> 00:21:55.790
That's right.

00:21:57.600 --> 00:21:59.290
W-what?

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:32.600
Good evening. Yamamoto here.

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:34.940
Thanks for all your help today, Anzu-chan.

00:23:34.940 --> 00:23:36.590
I appreciate it.

00:23:37.010 --> 00:23:39.620
You're next, Koume-chan.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:40.790
Okay.

00:23:40.790 --> 00:23:44.000
The next episode is about a detective and Koume's first love.

00:23:42.800 --> 00:23:43.780
"A Hanamaru Detective"

00:23:43.780 --> 00:23:44.790
"A Hanamaru First Love"

00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:44.790
Don't miss it.

00:23:44.790 --> 00:23:49.540
"See you next time!"
